I told the operator this item needs a native that constructs
`%struct.StructuredData`, including the compiled layout of `[]String` and `Map`.
That was WRONG, and this plan says so: step 1 mandates out-params and never a
struct-pointer return, with the reason documented — a struct-pointer return
silently couples LLVM struct layout to a hand-written #[repr(C)] and breaks on any
field reorder or pad change. The native returns the pieces; the LOWERING ARM builds
the struct. The ABI risk I described is therefore not present, and the correction is
recorded here rather than left in the transcript.

Added: the measured edit sites (interp arm at interp.rs:9959 — already correct and
the parity reference; the single facade at stdlib/browser.rs:35; the layout at
codegen.rs:1938-1955 whose field_kinds is load-bearing because all three fields
lower to I8Ptr and the kind alone routes `sd.json_ld.len` to the array count slot;
regex_ffi.rs as the FFI template and tallow_regex_is_match as the declare+call-arm
template), and why the remaining work is a fresh-session item: the codegen arm sits
on the interp/codegen byte-parity surface, there is no correctness defect to fix,
and a half-applied change there is worse than none.

Status: ready-for-agent, fully specified, not started.
